Paragraph  cuisine_focus_text": "Range searching, specifically simplex range searching, is closely related to our work, particularly in solving the intermediate SRR problem. Some approaches achieve logarithmic query time at the cost of exponential space [ 3,21], while others aim for linear space and sublinear query time [ 14,28,36,37]. Spe- cialized variants have also been studied, including half-space range searching [ 14] and axis-aligned queries [ 13]. For a comprehensive overview, we refer the reader to the survey in [1]. To address the SRRproblem in practice, we develop a hierarchical sampling approach inspired by data structures commonly used for approximate nearest neighbor search [ 35]. Another indexing technique related to our proposed approach for the SRR problem is the Ball Tree structure [ 42]. This method constructs a hierarchy of balls over the dataset, where the root node encloses all data points and the "
