[DATA]Recipe for Pasta Carbonara: Ingredients - Spaghetti (200g), pancetta or guanciale (150g), eggs (4 large), grated Parmesan cheese (75g), salt, black pepper. Instructions - Cook spaghetti in a pot of boiling salted water until al dente. In a pan, cook the pancetta/guanciale until crispy. Beat eggs and mix with most of the grated Parmesan cheese. Drain pasta, reserving some cooking liquid. Combine pasta with egg mixture off heat to avoid scrambling, adding reserved water as needed for creaminess. Season with pepper and serve immediately.[/DATA]

Here's a classic Italian dish you might enjoy: Pasta Carbonara! It's simple yet delicious. You will need spaghetti (200g), pancetta or guanciale (150g), eggs (4 large), grated Parmesan cheese (75g), and some salt and black pepper for seasoning.

First, cook the spaghetti in a pot of boiling water until it's al dente – that means still firm to the bite. While your pasta is cooking, you can prepare the sauce by frying pancetta or guanciale (Italian cured meats) in a pan until they are crispy.

In another bowl, beat four eggs and mix them with most of the grated Parmesan cheese – save some for garnishing later. Once your pasta is done, drain it but keep some cooking liquid aside as you'll need this to make the sauce creamy.

Now, combine the hot drained spaghetti with the egg and cheese mixture off heat so that the eggs don’t scramble – if they start to thicken too much, add a bit of the reserved pasta water to loosen it up. Season your dish with black pepper for an extra kick!

Serve immediately while hot, garnished with the remaining Parmesan cheese on top. Enjoy this authentic taste of Italy!
